review_comments:
This rotation doesn't strictly match stable, but making it match is probably more hassle than it is worth, as stable is using a somewhat complicated system of velocity and per-frame acceleration that is shared between osu! spinners and taiko swells. I'm gonna look away until someone complains that this is a problem.

That said, this method is missing two other transformations from stable:

```csharp
                SpriteCircleTop.Transformations.RemoveAll(t => t.Type == TransformationType.Scale);
                SpriteCircleTop.Transformations.Add(new Transformation(TransformationType.Scale, Math.Min(0.94f, SpriteCircleTop.Scale + 0.02f), 0.8f, AudioEngine.Time,
                                                                   AudioEngine.Time + 400, EasingTypes.Out));

                SpriteBonusCounter.Transformations.RemoveAll(t => t.Type == TransformationType.Scale);
                SpriteBonusCounter.Transformations.Add(new Transformation(TransformationType.Scale, SpriteBonusCounter.Scale, 1.6f - 0.6f * (float)rotationRequirement / totalRotationRequirement, AudioEngine.Time,
                                                                   AudioEngine.Time + 60, EasingTypes.Out));
```

`SpriteCircleTop` is `spinnerCircle`, and `SpriteBonusCounter` is `remainingHitsCountdown`.

Missing one more transform:

```csharp
                SpriteCircleTop.Transformations.RemoveAll(t => t.Type == TransformationType.Scale);
                SpriteCircleTop.Transformations.Add(new Transformation(TransformationType.Scale, SpriteCircleTop.Scale, SpriteCircleTop.Scale + 0.05f, AudioEngine.Time, AudioEngine.Time + 300, EasingTypes.Out));
```
